{
  "summary": "Adds UNIX domain socket support to the HTTP RPC server and bitcoin-cli using the `unix:<path>` format in `-rpcbind=` and `-rpcconnect=`. Introduces `UnixSocketAddr` and the variant type `SocketAddr` in `netbase` to decouple generic socket endpoints from P2P networking classes like `CService`, refactoring `Proxy` and `HTTPServer` to use them. Allows nodes to omit `-rpcallowip` when binding exclusively to UNIX sockets, relying on filesystem permissions for access control while retaining standard RPC user authentication.",
  "problem": "Local RPC communication currently relies on TCP loopback connections, which introduces TCP overhead and requires IP-based access filtering via `-rpcallowip` instead of standard OS filesystem permissions. Furthermore, previous UNIX socket support introduced for proxies left technical debt where socket abstractions were inconsistently integrated with P2P network classes.",
  "evidence": [
    "Closes long-standing issue #5029 (opened in 2014 requesting UNIX socket support for RPC).",
    "Author notes technical debt resolution: 'Back in #27375 we added unix socket support but it was isolated to the Proxy class. That created a bit of tech debt which we pay off in this PR.'"
  ],
